---
source: crates/cache-explorer-core/tests/golden.rs
description: "Store hits under write-back on direct-mapped-8: a clean line becomes dirty and memory stale; a dirty line is written again, once with a value memory already holds; then a store miss writes the dirty line back before it evicts it (cases 2, 5 and 7)."
---
1.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x0A4: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
1.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, compulsory | - | Set 2 is invalid. Miss.
1.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Set 2 has one way; the line goes there.
1.4 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x0A0–0x0AF from memory.
1.5 | complete | - | r1 | - | Read word 1 of way 0 (53) into r1.
2.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Store 0x0A4: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
2.2 | hit | associativity | accesses, stores, hits | - | Set 2, way 0: valid, and tag 0x01 matches. Hit.
2.3 | write | writePolicy | dirty 2/0, word 2/0/1 | - | Write 7 into word 1 of way 0 and set its dirty bit. Memory at 0x0A4 is now stale.
3.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Store 0x0A8: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 8 (word 2).
3.2 | hit | associativity | accesses, stores, hits | - | Set 2, way 0: valid, and tag 0x01 matches. Hit.
3.3 | write | writePolicy | word 2/0/2 | - | Write 9 into word 2 of way 0; the line was already dirty. Memory at 0x0A8 is stale.
4.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Store 0x0AC: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 12 (word 3).
4.2 | hit | associativity | accesses, stores, hits | - | Set 2, way 0: valid, and tag 0x01 matches. Hit.
4.3 | write | writePolicy | - | - | Write 79 into word 3 of way 0; the line was already dirty. Memory at 0x0AC already holds 79.
5.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x0B0: tag 0x01, set 3, offset 0 (word 0).
5.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, compulsory | - | Set 3 is invalid. Miss.
5.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Set 3 has one way; the line goes there.
5.4 | fill | lineSize | valid 3/0, tag 3/0, word 3/0/0, word 3/0/1, word 3/0/2, word 3/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x0B0–0x0BF from memory.
5.5 | complete | - | r1 | - | Read word 0 of way 0 (92) into r1.
6.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Store 0x0B0: tag 0x01, set 3, offset 0 (word 0).
6.2 | hit | associativity | accesses, stores, hits | - | Set 3, way 0: valid, and tag 0x01 matches. Hit.
6.3 | write | writePolicy | dirty 3/0 | - | Write 92 into word 0 of way 0 and set its dirty bit. Memory at 0x0B0 already holds 92.
7.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Store 0x1A4: tag 0x03, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
7.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, stores, misses, compulsory | - | Set 2 holds tag 0x01, not 0x03. Miss.
7.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Direct-mapped: way 0 is the only place for this line, so its current line must go.
7.4 | writeBack | writePolicy | memory 0xA4, memory 0xA8, writebacks | - | Way 0 is dirty: write line 0x0A0 back to memory first.
7.5 | evict | associativity | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, dirty 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, evictions | - | Evict line 0x0A0 (tag 0x01) from way 0.
7.6 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x1A0–0x1AF from memory.
7.7 | write | writePolicy | dirty 2/0, word 2/0/1 | - | Write 3 into word 1 of way 0 and set its dirty bit. Memory at 0x1A4 is now stale.
